course: dictionary
lesson: 4565
title: Hedgehogs in the garden
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hedgehog is a small wild animal with a pointed nose and a back covered in sharp spines. When it is frightened, it rolls into a ball, so the spines face outwards and keep it safe. Look for clues in the words around it to learn what it does and where it lives.
explain: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute.» Curled up means folded into a round shape, and the leaves tell you it is resting in a safe, cosy place. Breathing only a few times a minute tells you its body has slowed right down.
explain: «Loose garden netting can trap birds and hedgehogs, so it is kept tight or taken away.» Trap means catch so that an animal cannot get free. The word so shows the reason: people keep netting tight to stop hedgehogs getting caught.
fact: A hedgehog is a small wild animal with spines on its back.
fact: Hedgehogs live in gardens, hedges and woods in the UK, Ireland and New Zealand.
fact: Hedgehogs are nocturnal, which means they are active at night.
fact: Hedgehogs eat slugs, beetles and worms.
fact: In winter, a hedgehog hibernates: it sleeps deeply in a nest of leaves while its heart slows right down, from about 190 beats a minute to about 20.
exercise: «A hedgehog curled up in a pile of leaves in winter may breathe only a few times a minute.» What does the sentence tell us the hedgehog is doing in winter? | Building a nest out of stones | Walking through the snow looking for food | Swimming in the river | *Resting in a deep sleep while its body slows down
exercise: Where do hedgehogs live? | *In gardens, hedges and woods | In deserts and on mountain tops | Inside tall city towers | Deep under the sea
exercise: «Hedgehogs feed up in autumn, then hibernate in a nest of leaves.» Find and copy the word that means to sleep deeply through the cold winter. | *hibernate | feed | leaves | autumn
test: Hedgehogs are not native to which place? | Hedgehogs are not native to North America or Australia, so North America is the right answer. | Ireland | New Zealand is where they were brought in, so it is not native. Which is one of these? | Britain | *North America
test: What does a hedgehog do when it is frightened? | It runs away very fast over the lawn | It hides under the bed | *It rolls up into a ball | It climbs up the nearest tree
exam: Hedgehogs are nocturnal. What does nocturnal mean? | Active only in the morning | Able to swim very well | Covered in bright colours | *Active at night
